      "content": "It's exhausting when the well-meaning platitudes just feel empty, and your feeling of being unnoticed is a real, heavy thing. If the constant effort to be seen feels like too much right now, maybe the pressure to \"connect\" needs to be dropped entirely. Instead of forcing interactions, focus on finding one small, quiet thing that genuinely brings you comfort in your routine, even if it's just a book or a specific corner of the cafe. Letting go of the need for external validation can sometimes make the silence feel less oppressive.",
